{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I will give her her vineyards</b> — the opposite of \"and I will lay waste her vines.\"" "<b>And the Valley of Achor</b> — which I troubled, which is the Valley of Jezreel — shall become a Door of Hope." "<b>And she shall sing</b> — she will play and sing, like \"and Miriam answered them.\" Some say: she will vow there, derived from the root ענה, as written: \"and he answers islands in his widows\" [Job 9:26?], but this is far-fetched in my eyes."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "The citation 'וענה איים באלמנותיו' does not correspond clearly to any known biblical verse; it may be corrupt or an unusual paraphrase. Translated hyper-literally as quoted."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:54.780905043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}